    "parchment.crimson-dagger.passives.crimson-doom": "Whenever you slay a monster or have critical strike, gain one stack of Crimson Doom buff: improves critical chance and damage when attacking with this dagger by {0} and {1} respectively, for {2} seconds.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.abilities.unleashed": "For {0} seconds, Crimson Doom buff has no stack limit.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.hint1.vague": "There are ancient records about monsters worshipping so-called Lord of Death. They build statues in His favor. They even believed that He may grant a special boon to worthy ones.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.hint1.detailed": "In Quarry mine there is a statue of Grim Reaper. I believe it was built by followers of ancient monster religion that believed their God may grant a special weapons to worthy followers.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.hint2.vague": "These monsters worshipped by lighting braziers in their God's image. Records also say that to be granted the boon, you should part your ways with the most precious gem.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.hint2.detailed": "These monsters worshipped by lighting Skull braziers. You'd also need to bring a Prismatic shard so that He may notice you.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.hint3.vague": "But receiving said boon is not the ultimate sign of devotion. You'd need to collect enough items that resemble Him and a Galaxy Soul.",
    "parchment.crimson-dagger.hint3.detailed": "But it does not end on receiving this weapon. To prove your devotion, you should gather 6 various bone items and a Galaxy Soul to please your master.",
